## Phase 3: Production Deployment

### Option A: Deploy to Vercel (Recommended)

1. Push code to GitHub:
```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git remote add origin https://github.com/yourusername/genjex.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
```

2. Go to [vercel.com](https://vercel.com)
3. Click "Import Project"
4. Select your GitHub repository
5. Vercel will auto-detect Next.js configuration
6. Click Deploy
7. Your site will be live at `your-domain.vercel.app`

### Option B: Deploy to Netlify

1. Push code to GitHub (see above)
2. Go to [netlify.com](https://netlify.com)
3. Click "New site from Git"
4. Select your repository
5. Build command: `npm run build`
6. Publish directory: `.next`
7. Click Deploy

### Option C: Self-Hosted (VPS/Dedicated Server)

1. Build production bundle:
```bash
npm run build
```

2. Start production server:
```bash
npm start
```

3. Use PM2 for process management:
```bash
npm install -g pm2
pm2 start "npm start" --name genjex
```

4. Setup Nginx as reverse proxy pointing to `localhost:3000`
5. Configure SSL certificate (Let's Encrypt recommended)

